---
import CommandOptions from '../components/CommandOptions.astro';
import LiveQueue from '../components/LiveQueue.astro';
import ProductPost from '../components/ProductPost.astro';

const title = 'Workcell';
const description = 'A FIFO queue for the Macs, phones, GPUs, and rigs that coding agents share.';
const sourceUrl = 'https://github.com/jmonster/workcell/tree/main/workcell';
const agentInstructionsUrl = '/llms.txt';
const commandOptions = [
  {
    value: 'macos-xcode',
    summary: 'is the resource key.',
    detail: 'Matching keys take turns; different keys run independently.',
  },
  {
    value: '--wait',
    summary: 'waits in line until the command can run.',
    detail: 'Omit it to return immediately when the resource is busy.',
  },
  {
    value: '--json',
    summary: 'returns structured output.',
    detail: 'Includes the owner, queue position, log path, and a command for waiting.',
  },
];
---

<ProductPost
  title={title}
  description={description}
  product="workcell"
  sourceUrl={sourceUrl}
  agentInstructionsUrl={agentInstructionsUrl}
  publishedAt="2026-07-28T14:00:00-04:00"
  publishedLabel="Jul 28, 2026"
>
  <h2>What’s it for?</h2>

  <p class="drop-cap">Agents are easy to multiply. Hardware is not. Two builds can target the same Mac; two tests can reset the same phone; two jobs can claim the same GPU. One command can change the resource underneath another, and a green check may belong to the wrong run.</p>

  <p>Workcell gives each resource a first-in, first-out queue. One command owns it; the rest wait in order. When the owner exits, the next starts automatically. Jobs for other resources keep moving.</p>

  <div class="wide-demo" id="workcell">
    <LiveQueue id="workcell-live-queue" />
  </div>

  <h2 id="how-it-works">Install and use</h2>

  <pre><code>curl -fsSL https://workcell-137.pages.dev/install.sh | sh</code></pre>

  <h3>or tell your agent</h3>

  <pre><code>install https://workcell-137.pages.dev{agentInstructionsUrl}</code></pre>

  <p>then put Workcell in front of every command that needs <strong>the</strong> resource:</p>

  <pre><code>workcell run macos-xcode --wait -- xcodebuild test</code></pre>

  <CommandOptions items={commandOptions} />
</ProductPost>
